- chi_P U^2^4 = 1.674e-3, density p=0.168, so Q^2 := U^2^4/p^4 ≈ 2.10
- random Bernoulli matched: U^2^4 ≈ 8.5e-4 average, p ~ 0.17, Q^2 ≈ 1.06

So chi_P shows ratio ~2x — this looks like the Hardy-Littlewood box singular series. I need to compute the HL prediction analytically to compare. Let me add an HL computation module, then run the full experiment.
